marfrit-openvino (2026.4.0~dev20260821+p5-1) bookworm trixie; urgency=medium

  * One more patch applied on top of +p4, same upstream commit (71640275),
    same smallest-sufficient-divergence numbering:
    - patches/0019: the MoE per-expert prefill fallback's weight-side
      answer becomes three-way (no offload tier / device slot acquired or
      pinned / host tier). Patch 0018's single `false` meant both "no
      offload tier" and "not resident", and its caller took the host path
      for both -- on a resident-only load with both fast prefill paths
      forced off it downcast the resident provider to the offload one
      (undefined behaviour) for weights that were on the device. Dormant
      in every configuration arcint drives; closes the item 0018's own
      header reported. Red first with a new plugin unit test (the
      misrouted branch tried to map a weight file that does not exist),
      green with the patch, 21 of 21 MoE cases on both cards.
  * The runtime reports itself as 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29-marfrit-p5,
    so a version string in a log distinguishes this build from +p4 and
    from the stock nightly. Not yet built as a package at the time of
    this entry.

