marfrit-openvino (2026.4.0~dev20260821+p3-1) bookworm trixie; urgency=medium

  * Three more patches applied on top of +p2, same upstream commit
    (71640275), same smallest-sufficient-divergence numbering:
    - patches/0014: the GPU plugin's Assign adopts a same-type,
      same-rank output layout instead of asserting, closing the
      DFlash2 draft head's disable at prompts whose first draft
      concatenates exactly the state window's row count.
    - patches/0015: paged attention bounded partials — an f16 host
      sizing fix for the mixed-stage tmp_out buffer (it was allocating
      at 4 bytes/element for an already-f16 kernel output), a new
      read-write plugin property, PAGED_ATTENTION_MAX_PARTITIONS,
      bounding the online-merge partition count so the scratch term
      stops scaling with n_ctx past a fixed point, and the argument
      rebind fix: the implementation now records the identity of every
      intermediate its kernel arguments were bound to and forces a
      rebind when any changes, closing a use-after-free that only
      appears once the bound above makes the buffer's size plateau.
      Upgrade note: this option lands in the GPU model-cache blob's
      positionally serialised property schema — clear the GPU model
      cache (--cache-dir, if set) when upgrading to this level.
    - patches/0016: sizes the paged-attention intermediate buffers
      (exp_sums/max_logits/tmp_out) from the current call's partition
      count instead of reusing the previous call's, a stale-count
      hardening on top of 0015's corrected buffers.
    patches/README.md carries what each one is for and the measured
    numbers behind it.
  * The runtime reports itself as 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29-marfrit-p3,
    so a version string in a log distinguishes this build from +p2 and
    from the stock nightly.

